   "speech": "He gazed intently at the passers-by, who now and then glanced curiously at the white robe, the turban and the thin brown face of the Indian, with its motionless black eyes that stayed in the memory like a shout or a blow. So far Ranum had seen nothing out of the ordinary. Beneath a monotonous sameness of outward form there moved a procession of ordinary abominations; but among them, as the term of the awaited answer was running out, there passed someone in no way remarkable to our observation, yet astonishing to Ranum. He was about thirty; he was modestly dressed and healthy, with a pleasant, easy face and a firm step.",
